  { q: 'Are ravens smarter than crows?', a: 'Common Ravens and American Crows score similarly on most cognitive tasks. Ravens have shown slightly more flexible planning in some experiments; crows show more sophisticated tool use in others (the New Caledonian Crow especially). Both are exceptionally intelligent birds; the difference between them is small compared with the gap between corvids and most other birds.' },
